1
00:00:24,130 --> 00:00:27,040
She turned out that way 
because I wasn't with her.

2
00:00:28,350 --> 00:00:31,460
And I was going on about how 
I didn't want her to look sad...

3
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:35,130
Emilia, are you okay?

4
00:00:41,050 --> 00:00:42,270
<i>I'll save Emilia...</i>

5
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:45,720
<i>and the Sanctuary, and the mansion, too.</i>

6
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:48,020
<i>I'll save every last one of them,</i>

7
00:00:49,080 --> 00:00:51,010
<i>if it costs me my life.</i>

8
00:00:55,690 --> 00:00:57,500
Are you feeling all right?

9
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:01,450
Yes... because Subaru was 
there for me, I think.

10
00:01:01,890 --> 00:01:04,490
<i>The biggest problem is Roswaal.</i>

11
00:01:04,490 --> 00:01:07,450
<i>He knew that I've been looping,</i>

12
00:01:07,450 --> 00:01:10,670
<i>even if he didn't know that 
I have to die to do it.</i>

13
00:01:10,880 --> 00:01:14,380
<i>He's obviously following the Tome of Wisdom.</i>

14
00:01:14,690 --> 00:01:16,970
<i>He won't condone anything that 
goes against what's written,</i>

15
00:01:16,970 --> 00:01:20,930
<i>and if it does, he won't balk 
at using my loops to redo it.</i>

16
00:01:21,390 --> 00:01:23,890
<i>What's forcing him to do all that?</i>

17
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:26,850
<i>I...</i>

18
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:28,400
By doing that...

19
00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:32,150
you can become like me.

20
00:01:37,250 --> 00:01:39,140
<i>...won't ever be like you.</i>

21
00:01:39,690 --> 00:01:40,830
<i>Not ever.</i>

22
00:01:41,590 --> 00:01:44,660
<i>So... is it okay if I turn to you again?</i>

23
00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:50,880
<i>There are so many things I want to find 
out and get you to agonize over with me.</i>

24
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,670
Invite me, Echidna!

25
00:01:56,160 --> 00:01:58,530
I'll give you my life as many
times as you want it!

26
00:01:58,530 --> 00:02:01,220
Or my pride or anything else!

27
00:02:01,220 --> 00:02:03,180
So please, Echidna!

28
00:02:03,770 --> 00:02:04,680
Let me...

29
00:02:15,370 --> 00:02:17,650
<i>Behold an unthinkable present.</i>

30
00:02:18,410 --> 00:02:18,740
Huh?

31
00:02:21,660 --> 00:02:22,450
...iar.

32
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,130
Liar.

33
00:02:24,780 --> 00:02:27,370
Liar! Liar! Liar!

34
00:02:27,370 --> 00:02:31,580
Liar! Liar! Subaru, you liar!

35
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:30,120
<i>What... is this?</i>

36
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:31,580
Emilia-sama!

37
00:02:31,580 --> 00:02:33,820
You liar!

38
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:37,340
Subaru... Subaru... You liar...

39
00:02:36,890 --> 00:02:40,100
Felis! Come here at once! 
This is urgent! Hurry!

40
00:02:37,710 --> 00:02:40,570
You said... we'd be together...

41
00:02:40,570 --> 00:02:42,090
<i>I don't recognize this...</i>

42
00:02:42,490 --> 00:02:44,860
<i>I don't recognize this scenario.</i>

43
00:02:44,860 --> 00:02:45,690
Old Man Wil!

44
00:02:45,690 --> 00:02:47,220
<i>How could I recognize it?</i>

45
00:02:45,690 --> 00:02:49,200
His throat's been stabbed! 
We haven't a moment to lose!

46
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:54,900
<i>Stop... It's no use. He's already dead.</i>

47
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:56,110
I won't let you die!

48
00:02:56,530 --> 00:02:59,650
I won't let the one who 
saved me die in this way!

49
00:03:00,060 --> 00:03:02,340
Why did this have to happen now?

50
00:03:02,340 --> 00:03:05,030
Stop joking! Stop fooling around with us!

51
00:03:05,030 --> 00:03:09,220
<i>Stop it... Stop it! Stop it! 
Stop it! Stop it! Stop it!</i>

52
00:03:09,220 --> 00:03:13,370
It's too late. His soul is already gone.

53
00:03:13,370 --> 00:03:15,210
Why? Why?!

54
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:17,270
Why did you die so easily?

55
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:20,730
Subaru-dono, you are...

56
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:20,730
Weakling. Coward.

57
00:03:21,320 --> 00:03:23,830
You're leaving behind everyone you cared about,

58
00:03:23,830 --> 00:03:27,500
forcing all of the pain and suffering on us.

59
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:30,560
You said...

60
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:36,020
You said... that you loved me.

61
00:03:43,860 --> 00:03:44,920
Was that...

62
00:03:52,170 --> 00:03:56,250
...how that world looked after I died?

63
00:03:56,970 --> 00:04:00,970
Or was it the trial? Not really my past,
 but the second trial?

64
00:04:01,450 --> 00:04:03,790
<i>Behold an unthinkable present.</i>

65
00:04:14,410 --> 00:04:16,020
Subaru?

66
00:04:16,020 --> 00:04:18,080
Emilia-sama, please...

67
00:04:18,650 --> 00:04:21,200
Wipe Subaru's face for him.

68
00:04:25,620 --> 00:04:26,690
Why?

69
00:04:27,390 --> 00:04:29,850
Why does Subaru look like this?

70
00:04:30,940 --> 00:04:34,000
Why did this have to happen to him?

71
00:04:34,490 --> 00:04:36,260
To save me?

72
00:04:37,150 --> 00:04:39,710
Why? Please tell me.

73
00:04:40,200 --> 00:04:45,650
I wanted to speak with
you more, Natsuki Subaru.

74
00:04:50,310 --> 00:04:53,890
I wanted to call you a friend.

75
00:05:01,830 --> 00:05:03,680
Stop... it...

76
00:05:04,730 --> 00:05:05,650
Please...

77
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:07,500
Stop it!

78
00:05:10,630 --> 00:05:12,900
<i>Behold an unthinkable present.</i>

79
00:05:17,610 --> 00:05:21,800
After all that nonsense you kept spouting...

80
00:05:27,390 --> 00:05:31,900
Was this all part of your 
plan as well, Beatrice-sama?

81
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:34,060
Why?

82
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:39,590
I knew you couldn't be "that person."

83
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:41,770
But still...

84
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:48,490
This is what you call "love"? Honestly...

85
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:50,490
There's no help for you.

86
00:05:51,070 --> 00:05:53,160
<i>Behold an unthinkable present.</i>

87
00:05:56,220 --> 00:05:57,940
So it is you.

88
00:06:04,810 --> 00:06:09,300
Emilia-sama and Subaru are 
both gone now, aren't they?

89
00:06:09,570 --> 00:06:12,270
Lia is asleep. Forever.

90
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:16,100
I don't want to exist in a world without her.

91
00:06:16,650 --> 00:06:21,440
Therefore, per our contract, 
I will freeze this world solid.

92
00:06:22,180 --> 00:06:25,150
He and I are equally guilty.

93
00:06:25,420 --> 00:06:30,030
And that is why you're trying 
to destroy the world?

94
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:33,950
I am going to stop you from 
causing any further harm.

95
00:06:34,550 --> 00:06:36,780
If you must resent someone, please resent me.

96
00:06:37,350 --> 00:06:39,540
I don't resent anyone, Reinhard.

97
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:43,380
You are a true hero.

98
00:06:43,990 --> 00:06:45,920
And a hero is all you can be.

99
00:06:55,890 --> 00:06:58,310
<i>Behold an unthinkable present.</i>

100
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:03,100
And that's the end of it.

101
00:07:03,100 --> 00:07:06,170
This wasn't a very rewarding job at all.

102
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:09,240
<i>Behold an unthinkable present.</i>

103
00:07:10,030 --> 00:07:12,360
I only prevented the situation from worsening.

104
00:07:12,770 --> 00:07:16,260
I could tell that Subaru-kun 
was already beyond help.

105
00:07:16,260 --> 00:07:19,120
Surely he wanted me to end 
it as quickly as possible.

106
00:07:16,860 --> 00:07:19,120
<i>Behold an unthinkable present.</i>

107
00:07:19,580 --> 00:07:21,830
<i>Behold an unthinkable present.</i>

108
00:07:21,960 --> 00:07:24,080
<i>Behold an unthinkable present.</i>

109
00:07:24,210 --> 00:07:26,210
<i>Behold an unthinkable present.</i>

110
00:07:26,410 --> 00:07:28,380
<i>Behold an unthinkable present.</i>

111
00:07:28,380 --> 00:07:29,960
<i>Behold an unthinkable present.</i>

112
00:07:29,960 --> 00:07:31,320
<i>Behold an unthinkable present.</i>

113
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:33,690
<i>Behold an unthinkable present.</i>

114
00:07:33,690 --> 00:07:35,980
<i>Behold an unthinkable present.</i>

115
00:07:43,220 --> 00:07:47,510
Can you no longer stand, Subaru-kun?

116
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:56,430
This can't be real.

117
00:07:56,430 --> 00:07:57,870
It is real.

118
00:07:58,280 --> 00:08:02,470
I will be by your side whenever 
you wish it, Subaru-kun.

119
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:04,670
Rem...

120
00:08:04,670 --> 00:08:07,670
Yes. I am your Rem.

121
00:08:13,990 --> 00:08:14,840
Rem...

122
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:16,820
Yes, I am Rem.

123
00:08:16,820 --> 00:08:20,680
Your very own, all-purpose, 
ever-useful maid.

124
00:08:21,050 --> 00:08:22,390
You...

125
00:08:22,910 --> 00:08:25,940
Are you all right? Are you tired?

126
00:08:27,200 --> 00:08:28,270
I don't know...

127
00:08:29,430 --> 00:08:31,360
Maybe I am tired.

128
00:08:32,280 --> 00:08:34,580
But I haven't even done anything yet...

129
00:08:36,220 --> 00:08:41,900
If I were stronger, smarter, 
and capable of a lot more,

130
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:47,080
they wouldn't have had to 
hurt and suffer so much.

131
00:08:47,760 --> 00:08:49,040
Subaru-kun...

132
00:08:49,490 --> 00:08:52,940
If the world was still going on after I died,

133
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:56,050
how many times did I just 
leave them all to die?

134
00:08:56,590 --> 00:08:57,510
Subaru-kun...

135
00:08:57,790 --> 00:09:00,920
How many times did I let you die?

136
00:09:01,880 --> 00:09:04,640
How many times do I have to kill you?!

137
00:09:04,640 --> 00:09:05,980
Subaru-kun.

138
00:09:08,510 --> 00:09:10,020
It's all right.

139
00:09:10,620 --> 00:09:11,340
Rem...

140
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:13,230
I love you.

141
00:09:14,570 --> 00:09:16,660
I love you, Subaru-kun.

142
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:20,030
So everything will be all right.

143
00:09:20,470 --> 00:09:23,990
Th-That doesn't... answer anything...

144
00:09:23,990 --> 00:09:25,220
It does.

145
00:09:25,670 --> 00:09:29,000
Holding you the way I am right now

146
00:09:29,690 --> 00:09:31,210
is the answer to everything.

147
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:35,060
You've been through so much, Subaru-kun.

148
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:37,960
You suffered so much pain all alone...

149
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:42,540
But you don't need to feel 
so sad all the time anymore.

150
00:09:43,210 --> 00:09:44,310
I...

151
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:48,180
I will take the place of 
everything you're feeling.

152
00:09:48,740 --> 00:09:52,070
Just entrust everything to me,

153
00:09:52,070 --> 00:09:54,030
and just rest for now.

154
00:09:54,610 --> 00:09:56,570
All you need to do is sleep.

155
00:10:04,180 --> 00:10:05,110
Rem...

156
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:08,840
<i>It's easy to give up.</i>

157
00:10:08,840 --> 00:10:11,860
<i>But it doesn't suit you.</i>

158
00:10:13,700 --> 00:10:15,560
Who are you?

159
00:10:15,560 --> 00:10:16,400
Huh?

160
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:19,300
I'm asking you who you are.

161
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:21,890
S-Subaru-kun, what are you—

162
00:10:21,890 --> 00:10:24,800
I knew that when I was at the end of my rope,

163
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:27,640
clutching my knees and wallowing in anguish,

164
00:10:28,290 --> 00:10:31,520
you would come and stay gently by my side.

165
00:10:32,020 --> 00:10:36,320
You'd listen to my troubles, 
let me vent my insecurities,

166
00:10:36,760 --> 00:10:39,610
and wring everything out of 
me until my tears ran dry...

167
00:10:40,010 --> 00:10:43,830
And then you'd say, "Now, stand up."

168
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:48,060
You wouldn't tell me to just rest.

169
00:10:48,060 --> 00:10:51,120
You wouldn't tell me to give up 
and entrust everything to you.

170
00:10:51,670 --> 00:10:54,200
You like me and I like you,

171
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:56,960
you're good to me and you love me,

172
00:10:56,960 --> 00:10:59,130
but you're also stricter 
with me than anyone else.

173
00:10:59,730 --> 00:11:02,260
Rem is the one girl who doesn't go easy on me!

174
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:05,190
You're wrong! Please listen 
to me, Subaru-kun!

175
00:11:05,190 --> 00:11:06,800
I just don't want to see you suffering so—

176
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:10,540
I'll show you my weakness and my fragility.

177
00:11:10,540 --> 00:11:13,190
But I'll never let you see me give up!

178
00:11:13,460 --> 00:11:15,860
Because you are my hero, Subaru-kun!

179
00:11:16,220 --> 00:11:18,280
Get out of here, you fraud!

180
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:23,200
Don't you dare coddle me 
with Rem's face and voice!

181
00:11:25,060 --> 00:11:31,670
Th-This isn't... what I... 
was told... t-to expect...

182
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:32,620
Huh?

183
00:11:42,310 --> 00:11:44,130
And who are you?

184
00:11:44,130 --> 00:11:48,780
I-I'm Carmilla, th-the Witch of Lust.

185
00:11:48,780 --> 00:11:50,620
N-Nice to meet... you...

186
00:11:50,620 --> 00:11:54,310
Is this weird place part of Echidna's dream?

187
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:57,560
What were you trying to pull earlier?!

188
00:11:57,960 --> 00:11:59,280
Earlier?

189
00:11:59,660 --> 00:12:02,550
I'm talking about you coming 
to me disguised as Rem!

190
00:12:02,550 --> 00:12:04,200
Was that your power?!

191
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:05,810
N-No!

192
00:12:05,810 --> 00:12:09,290
I-If I looked like s-someone else,

193
00:12:09,290 --> 00:12:13,540
it's because... y-you wanted 
to see me that way...

194
00:12:13,540 --> 00:12:14,250
What?!

195
00:12:14,630 --> 00:12:18,770
I-I didn't w-want to, but Echidna-chan said

196
00:12:18,770 --> 00:12:20,750
a-all I had to do was dote on you...

197
00:12:20,750 --> 00:12:22,840
So Echidna <i>is</i> the one behind all this?!

198
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:25,260
Going any further will endanger your life.

199
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:35,040
Carmilla's "Faceless Bride"

200
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:37,900
makes one forget to breathe 
when in her presence.

201
00:12:38,320 --> 00:12:41,740
In the end, it even makes 
your heart stop beating.

202
00:12:42,290 --> 00:12:46,660
What the hell have you been plotting, Echidna?

203
00:12:46,660 --> 00:12:48,110
Isn't that obvious?

204
00:12:48,110 --> 00:12:50,570
An evil scheme, of course. I <i>am</i> a witch.

205
00:12:51,320 --> 00:12:52,870
Why did you do something like that?

206
00:12:53,390 --> 00:12:57,580
Because it was the most 
effective method, that's why.

207
00:12:57,580 --> 00:12:59,240
If I'd left things alone,

208
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:02,880
your mind would've worn away 
to nothing in the trial.

209
00:13:03,490 --> 00:13:06,130
So you're telling me you did that to save me?

210
00:13:07,160 --> 00:13:11,570
I can't make any excuses for the fact 
that I wounded your heart as a result.

211
00:13:11,570 --> 00:13:13,480
I've resigned myself to accepting your rage.

212
00:13:22,880 --> 00:13:26,320
I know what it is you want to know 
more than anything right now.

213
00:13:26,930 --> 00:13:28,780
Allow me to explain the trial.

214
00:13:29,740 --> 00:13:31,840
Just like the first one,

215
00:13:31,840 --> 00:13:35,850
the second trial puts you in a world 
recreated from your memories.

216
00:13:36,260 --> 00:13:38,950
It's a thoroughly 
well-constructed unreality.

217
00:13:40,500 --> 00:13:41,220
Then—

218
00:13:41,220 --> 00:13:42,050
However...

219
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:46,030
Your Return by Death is the 
Witch of Envy's Authority.

220
00:13:46,030 --> 00:13:50,640
Basically, only she knows 
whether the things you saw

221
00:13:50,640 --> 00:13:53,520
in your second trial happened in some reality.

222
00:13:53,980 --> 00:13:58,510
You mean all that stuff might 
have actually happened?

223
00:13:58,510 --> 00:14:00,750
I'm only saying it's a possibility.

224
00:14:01,140 --> 00:14:04,120
Instead of counting the many people 
you may have failed to save,

225
00:14:04,120 --> 00:14:07,290
you should focus on counting 
the many you have saved.

226
00:14:07,290 --> 00:14:09,110
Idealistic clichés like that don't help!

227
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:13,120
I know that you have given 
all of your strength,

228
00:14:13,120 --> 00:14:16,540
physical and mental, to survive thus far.

229
00:14:17,520 --> 00:14:22,430
Not a single thing you've experienced on 
your way to this point has been a waste.

230
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:26,800
You have arrived at this moment by 
doing everything in your power,

231
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:28,590
at the risk of your own life.

232
00:14:29,440 --> 00:14:32,010
That's something you should be proud of.

233
00:14:33,820 --> 00:14:38,940
Why do you keep trying to help me like this?

234
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:46,280
I think it's a little mean to force 
a girl to spell that out for you.

235
00:14:49,780 --> 00:14:54,750
Would you be willing to form a 
contract with me, Natsuki Subaru?

236
00:14:55,810 --> 00:14:57,360
A contract?

237
00:14:57,360 --> 00:15:01,060
Yes, a formal contract with the Witch of Greed.

238
00:15:01,060 --> 00:15:03,700
Would you enter into one with me?

239
00:15:04,860 --> 00:15:06,880
What happens if I do?

240
00:15:07,360 --> 00:15:08,920
It's very simple.

241
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:13,090
From now on, whenever you run into 
an obstacle you can't overcome,

242
00:15:13,090 --> 00:15:15,900
when you feel you're being crushed 
by the weight of your sins,

243
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:18,010
I will give you my support.

244
00:15:18,010 --> 00:15:20,310
I'm confident in the amount 
of knowledge I have.

245
00:15:20,310 --> 00:15:23,680
I should be able to come up with a way 
for you to deal with any problem.

246
00:15:23,680 --> 00:15:27,660
Above all, I can share in your 
Return by Death ability.

247
00:15:28,070 --> 00:15:29,440
What does that mean?

248
00:15:30,010 --> 00:15:33,370
You're actually telling me the selling 
points of making a contract with you?

249
00:15:33,730 --> 00:15:37,320
I think it only makes sense to 
explain the merits of such an act.

250
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:41,260
All the better for me if it makes you 
lean toward agreeing to it at all.

251
00:15:41,640 --> 00:15:42,750
It's all calculated.

252
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:54,220
That might not be such a bad idea.

253
00:15:54,220 --> 00:15:55,470
Meaning?!

254
00:15:57,950 --> 00:16:00,220
I mean, uh... right.

255
00:16:00,220 --> 00:16:03,940
If you absolutely insist, I wouldn't 
mind entering into a contract—

256
00:16:03,940 --> 00:16:05,730
It's a little late to try and play it cool now!

257
00:16:06,230 --> 00:16:09,810
Anyway, how would we form this contract?

258
00:16:09,810 --> 00:16:12,110
To establish a formal contract,

259
00:16:12,110 --> 00:16:15,740
you and I need to form
a bond between our souls.

260
00:16:16,300 --> 00:16:19,460
First, we raise our palms 
to each other, like this.

261
00:16:29,380 --> 00:16:30,780
Wh-Wha?!

262
00:16:34,960 --> 00:16:36,540
I'm gonna have to...

263
00:16:37,510 --> 00:16:39,030
put a stop to that contract.

264
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:42,180
The Witch of Wrath?!

265
00:16:42,610 --> 00:16:44,100
I won't accept it!

266
00:16:44,550 --> 00:16:46,800
So you're after him, too?

267
00:16:46,800 --> 00:16:48,480
I suppose you're jealous.

268
00:16:48,480 --> 00:16:50,240
Stop teasing me!

269
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:53,870
I'm outraged! I'm indignant!

270
00:16:53,870 --> 00:16:56,560
I'm absolutely boiling with anger!

271
00:16:56,560 --> 00:16:58,800
How is she even here?

272
00:16:58,800 --> 00:17:02,800
Don't you have to swap places with the 
other witches to let them appear?

273
00:17:02,800 --> 00:17:03,960
That's a lie!

274
00:17:04,190 --> 00:17:08,330
She's a bad-natured jerk who plays 
mean tricks like that for no reason!

275
00:17:09,630 --> 00:17:12,320
Well, I didn't want to just keep 
popping witches into existence,

276
00:17:12,320 --> 00:17:15,030
and let one of them take you from me.

277
00:17:15,030 --> 00:17:19,380
Stop being taken in so easily by 
all of Echidna's smooth-talking!

278
00:17:19,380 --> 00:17:20,680
It pisses me off!

279
00:17:20,680 --> 00:17:23,390
Also, she hasn't even told you 
what parts of that contract...

280
00:17:23,390 --> 00:17:24,280
would be...

281
00:17:24,280 --> 00:17:25,000
bad...

282
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,480
for you!

283
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:29,020
H-Hang on! "Bad" for me?!

284
00:17:29,020 --> 00:17:32,010
She's talking about your payment 
for contracting with me.

285
00:17:32,010 --> 00:17:35,860
I think calling it a bad thing is 
a bit of an exaggeration, though.

286
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:39,160
What is it you want from me, then?

287
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:41,180
What payment do I have to give?

288
00:17:41,670 --> 00:17:43,080
It's very simple.

289
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:47,310
Everything you feel, everything you think,

290
00:17:47,310 --> 00:17:49,440
everything that remains in your heart,

291
00:17:49,440 --> 00:17:51,230
the future as you know it,

292
00:17:51,230 --> 00:17:52,950
anything you accomplish,

293
00:17:52,950 --> 00:17:55,110
all the potential within you,

294
00:17:55,110 --> 00:17:59,580
all the fruit of the unknown that 
is borne from your very existence...

295
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:03,390
I want a taste of it.

296
00:18:05,120 --> 00:18:08,040
Th-That's all true...

297
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:12,310
B-But don't assume that she 
just t-told you everything...

298
00:18:12,310 --> 00:18:13,820
The Witch of Lust?

299
00:18:13,820 --> 00:18:18,800
E-Echidna-chan... isn't lying...

300
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:21,280
But there's a lot... she's hiding from you.

301
00:18:21,720 --> 00:18:25,940
Don't bother listening to 
these two, Natsuki Subaru.

302
00:18:26,410 --> 00:18:28,790
Once you have formed a contract with me,

303
00:18:29,290 --> 00:18:33,750
I will, without fail, guide you
 to the future you desire.

304
00:18:34,160 --> 00:18:38,920
This wouldn't be the promise you always 
precede with "In the end..." would it?

305
00:18:39,970 --> 00:18:41,860
And who are you?!

306
00:18:41,860 --> 00:18:44,230
The Witch of Sloth, Sekhmet.

307
00:18:45,760 --> 00:18:48,450
Just letting you know my name, 
for the record and all.

308
00:18:49,210 --> 00:18:50,810
You're the sixth...

309
00:18:51,100 --> 00:18:56,580
I'm only here as a watchdog to 
preserve the fairness of this place.

310
00:18:57,810 --> 00:19:00,820
But I will fulfill my obligation to her.

311
00:19:01,510 --> 00:19:03,320
Oh, Baru, you're here?

312
00:19:03,320 --> 00:19:06,950
Is everyone here now? That's unusual!

313
00:19:07,800 --> 00:19:10,570
It's been a long time since we had a tea party.

314
00:19:10,570 --> 00:19:12,670
You should have invited me, too.

315
00:19:12,670 --> 00:19:15,350
Why do you guys keep appearing 
one after another?!

316
00:19:15,350 --> 00:19:16,840
What do you want from me?!

317
00:19:16,840 --> 00:19:18,600
I believe I told you already.

318
00:19:19,320 --> 00:19:23,420
It's the promise that's always 
preceded by "In the end..."

319
00:19:25,220 --> 00:19:27,420
"In the end"?

320
00:19:30,700 --> 00:19:37,840
Echidna, you said you'd guide me to 
the best possible future, didn't you?

321
00:19:37,840 --> 00:19:40,830
Yes, I did. It was true.

322
00:19:40,830 --> 00:19:44,530
And with your help, would I arrive 
at the best possible future

323
00:19:44,940 --> 00:19:47,520
by following the best possible path?

324
00:19:50,120 --> 00:19:51,690
Why aren't you saying anything?

325
00:19:52,460 --> 00:19:54,000
Answer me, Echidna!

326
00:19:56,940 --> 00:19:59,880
Answer me, Witch of Greed!

327
00:20:02,500 --> 00:20:05,100
For the purpose of attaining 
the future you desire,

328
00:20:05,100 --> 00:20:08,180
you must accept any sacrifices 
made along the way.

329
00:20:08,180 --> 00:20:13,060
Is that not the resolution 
you made, Natsuki Subaru?

330
00:20:13,670 --> 00:20:15,670
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait!

331
00:20:15,670 --> 00:20:17,480
No, I will not wait.

332
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:19,480
You are the one who needs 
to understand better.

333
00:20:19,840 --> 00:20:21,110
Just think about it!

334
00:20:21,500 --> 00:20:25,170
The Return by Death Authority you 
possess is a tremendous thing.

335
00:20:25,170 --> 00:20:28,100
You do not fully understand 
how truly useful it is.

336
00:20:28,100 --> 00:20:32,230
It allows you to restart the world all you 
want until you reach your desired future.

337
00:20:32,230 --> 00:20:35,880
It's the embodiment of the ultimate 
ideal any seeker could wish for!

338
00:20:36,340 --> 00:20:39,950
Of course, I won't force 
you to Return by Death.

339
00:20:39,950 --> 00:20:43,250
You will use it to achieve 
the result you desire,

340
00:20:43,250 --> 00:20:47,600
and I will lend you all the wisdom 
you need to fulfill your wish.

341
00:20:47,940 --> 00:20:50,690
I expect all the results that 
come about in the process

342
00:20:50,690 --> 00:20:54,850
to contribute vastly to the 
satisfaction of my curiosity!

343
00:20:55,170 --> 00:20:59,160
We will agonize over, struggle with, 
and solve the same problems together.

344
00:20:59,160 --> 00:21:01,990
We will have the optimal 
relationship to achieve that!

345
00:21:02,340 --> 00:21:04,270
As I make use of your power,

346
00:21:04,270 --> 00:21:08,020
I want you to use me to achieve your 
best possible future, too.

347
00:21:08,020 --> 00:21:13,200
My maidenly heart's affection for you 
and desire to help you are real.

348
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:16,080
I'd be more than content to have 
you treat me as a convenience.

349
00:21:16,080 --> 00:21:20,130
If it's what you want, you're welcome 
to use my body for your comfort!

350
00:21:20,600 --> 00:21:22,130
I gladly offer it to you!

351
00:21:22,600 --> 00:21:26,150
I will give you the strength to 
move forward with my words.

352
00:21:26,150 --> 00:21:28,500
Whether you want comfort, 
motivation, or love,

353
00:21:28,500 --> 00:21:32,660
or even hatred, I will give it 
all to you. I can give it all!

354
00:21:33,060 --> 00:21:35,020
You like girls who give you 
everything, don't you?

355
00:21:35,260 --> 00:21:37,060
You need me!

356
00:21:37,300 --> 00:21:40,610
No one but you can satisfy 
my curiosity now.

357
00:21:40,610 --> 00:21:43,330
If you use your power to save someone,

358
00:21:43,330 --> 00:21:44,930
I want you to save me.

359
00:21:44,930 --> 00:21:48,080
I cannot control my own greed!

360
00:21:48,080 --> 00:21:52,540
No matter what happens, I will guide 
you to the future you desire.

361
00:21:52,540 --> 00:21:54,950
I swear it! I absolutely swear it!

362
00:21:54,950 --> 00:21:57,420
And the Sanctuary's liberation 
lies beyond that.

363
00:21:57,420 --> 00:22:02,300
You can save everyone trapped there—the one
 you love and all those you care about!

364
00:22:02,500 --> 00:22:05,160
For that purpose, I want 
you to take me, use me,

365
00:22:05,160 --> 00:22:07,310
and rob me of all the greed you want,

366
00:22:07,310 --> 00:22:08,740
so we can take hold of our future!

367
00:22:08,740 --> 00:22:10,720
That is all I want from you, 
all I desire from you,

368
00:22:10,720 --> 00:22:13,900
and all I offer in return.

369
00:22:13,900 --> 00:22:19,130
I have now told you everything... truly, 
every last detail, with passion.

370
00:22:19,130 --> 00:22:22,500
This might be close to love.
 It's a vow of love!

371
00:22:22,500 --> 00:22:24,990
And how will you respond to my love?

372
00:22:24,990 --> 00:22:26,190
I want your answer!

373
00:22:26,190 --> 00:22:30,340
That is one of the answers that will 
satisfy my curiosity, after all.

374
00:22:36,540 --> 00:22:37,550
Echidna...

375
00:22:37,550 --> 00:22:38,830
Yes?

376
00:22:38,830 --> 00:22:41,680
You're going to use me?

377
00:22:41,680 --> 00:22:42,680
I am.

378
00:22:42,680 --> 00:22:44,720
And you can do the same to me.

379
00:22:44,720 --> 00:22:46,500
That's what this contract is for.

380
00:22:46,860 --> 00:22:49,430
If you want to criticize 
me for using it as a means

381
00:22:49,430 --> 00:22:52,170
to keep you as my own, I'll accept that.

382
00:22:52,170 --> 00:22:53,300
It's the truth, after all.

383
00:22:54,870 --> 00:22:57,090
It's not as if I never considered

384
00:22:57,670 --> 00:23:00,670
that your intentions might not be 100% good.

385
00:23:01,880 --> 00:23:06,900
But... that's just way beyond the pale!

386
00:23:09,460 --> 00:23:13,370
I don't quite understand what 
you find so problematic.

387
00:23:13,880 --> 00:23:17,330
Everything about your attitude 
is so infantile and shallow!

388
00:23:17,330 --> 00:23:19,730
It's all completely superficial!

389
00:23:19,730 --> 00:23:23,380
When you laugh, even when 
you're mad, your attitude is...

390
00:23:24,440 --> 00:23:29,290
Echidna, you're incapable of 
understanding how anyone else feels!

391
00:23:30,910 --> 00:23:33,490
This is one of those times 
when you could get angry...

392
00:23:35,120 --> 00:23:37,620
I see. You have taught me much.

393
00:23:38,640 --> 00:23:40,440
When we next have a chance...

394
00:23:41,180 --> 00:23:42,770
I will do just that.

395
00:23:46,860 --> 00:23:48,770
But first, why not have a seat?

396
00:23:48,770 --> 00:23:51,740
I'd like to discuss our contract a bit more.

397
00:23:52,400 --> 00:23:53,410
I just remembered...

398
00:23:53,950 --> 00:23:57,560
There was one thing I wanted to 
ask you when I saw you again.

399
00:23:57,560 --> 00:23:59,420
Oh? What might that be?

400
00:23:59,420 --> 00:24:03,420
Once I hear your answer, I think 
I'll be able to make a choice.

401
00:24:05,390 --> 00:24:07,090
You know Beatrice, don't you?

402
00:24:07,450 --> 00:24:08,770
Yes, I do.

403
00:24:08,770 --> 00:24:12,260
I was deeply involved in her birth, after all.

404
00:24:12,900 --> 00:24:14,840
Beatrice has lived her life under a contract

405
00:24:14,840 --> 00:24:17,360
forcing her to wait for "that person."

406
00:24:17,360 --> 00:24:20,600
I believe that contract was with you.

407
00:24:20,600 --> 00:24:22,830
True. I'm the one who ordered her to protect

408
00:24:22,830 --> 00:24:26,010
the forbidden library and await 
the one who would come for her.

409
00:24:26,010 --> 00:24:28,970
Then who is "that person"?

410
00:24:28,970 --> 00:24:30,820
How can I set her free?

411
00:24:37,430 --> 00:24:40,330
Good question! Whoever could it be?

412
00:24:41,790 --> 00:24:42,680
What?!

413
00:24:43,960 --> 00:24:48,300
You... You're saying you don't even 
know who Beatrice is waiting for?!

414
00:24:48,300 --> 00:24:49,670
I really don't know.

415
00:24:50,160 --> 00:24:51,380
But why?

416
00:24:51,870 --> 00:24:54,320
Weren't you the one who told 
her to wait for them?!

417
00:24:54,320 --> 00:24:56,820
You've made quite a misunderstanding.

418
00:24:57,240 --> 00:25:00,410
I didn't force Beatrice to make that promise

419
00:25:00,410 --> 00:25:02,600
so she'd give the forbidden 
library to "that person."

420
00:25:03,030 --> 00:25:03,560
What?

421
00:25:04,040 --> 00:25:06,620
That wasn't my goal at all.

422
00:25:07,020 --> 00:25:11,470
By making her promise to wait for 
"that person" to come to her,

423
00:25:11,470 --> 00:25:14,350
I want to find out who she will choose

424
00:25:14,950 --> 00:25:16,860
to be "that person."

425
00:25:18,990 --> 00:25:23,810
Of course, her staying there for 400 years 
without choosing anyone is one result of that.

426
00:25:23,810 --> 00:25:27,080
Her inability to choose anyone 
so easily all this time

427
00:25:27,080 --> 00:25:31,360
and wanting to die as she agonized over 
whether to keep upholding the contract or not

428
00:25:31,360 --> 00:25:32,900
are also results of that.

429
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:36,720
And how do you feel about that?

430
00:25:39,940 --> 00:25:42,430
I think it's wonderful.

431
00:25:42,850 --> 00:25:44,430
Echidna...

432
00:25:45,510 --> 00:25:47,350
You are a witch!

433
00:25:48,760 --> 00:25:52,260
You're an unfathomable monster 
beyond all comprehension!

434
00:25:53,350 --> 00:25:54,410
And I...

435
00:25:55,000 --> 00:25:57,240
I won't take your hand.

436
00:25:58,160 --> 00:26:00,740
I know whose hand I want to take.

437
00:26:02,080 --> 00:26:05,640
There's a girl who's been 
tied down by the words

438
00:26:05,640 --> 00:26:08,120
you spoke out of pure
curiosity, without malice.

439
00:26:11,880 --> 00:26:13,350
My mind's made up.

440
00:26:13,350 --> 00:26:15,490
I'm going to take <i>her</i> hand.

441
00:26:15,490 --> 00:26:17,180
I won't go with you.

442
00:26:25,750 --> 00:26:26,430
She's here.

443
00:26:26,650 --> 00:26:27,880
N-No!

444
00:26:27,880 --> 00:26:30,470
I have nothing to do with any of this!

445
00:26:29,450 --> 00:26:33,910
A really troublesome girl just showed up 
at a troubling time to start some trouble.

446
00:26:34,570 --> 00:26:39,160
Oh! I'm feeling very, very hungry!

447
00:26:44,350 --> 00:26:46,250
Hey! It's Tella!

448
00:26:46,460 --> 00:26:48,500
Long time no see!

449
00:26:56,880 --> 00:26:59,880
The Witches' Tea Party

450
00:26:58,500 --> 00:27:08,500


